  "id": "COMPOUND:5613 - PROTEIN:717",
  "verbalization": "Sibrotuzumab appears to interact with the ATP-binding cassette sub-family C member 9 (ABCC9) through a series of molecular targets, all of which are involved in metabolic pathways. The evidence suggests that Sibrotuzumab targets Arginine deiminase, a enzyme that catalyzes the conversion of arginine to citrulline, and this enzyme in turn targets multiple compounds, including Conferol and Ligustrone A, which ultimately interact with ABCC9. These findings imply that Sibrotuzumab may modulate the activity of ABCC9 through a chain of metabolic intermediates, potentially influencing cellular processes related to drug resistance or transport functions. The consistent presence of these targets across different paths indicates a plausible mechanism of action, though the exact nature of the interaction between Sibrotuzumab and ABCC9 remains to be fully elucidated.",
